<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Uparika</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as uparikas</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">An uparika was a provincial governor in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gupta-empire">Gupta Empire</a>. The Gupta Empire profile explains that the empire was divided into provinces called <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bhukti">bhuktis</a>, each administered by an uparika, frequently a member of the royal family. Below them, districts called <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vishaya">vishayas</a> were managed by officials known as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vishayapati">vishayapatis</a>.</p></div>
